%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:vegas -- after a timeout, Vegas restarts with a window of two segments.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; TcpVegas is the
algorithm of Brakmo and Peterson.

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates TcpVegas: after a timeout, TcpNewReno, TcpReno, DcTcp and TcpCubic
restart with one segment of data, TcpTahoe and TcpWestwood with one MSS, and
TcpNoCongestionControl and DumbTcp have no window.

Host under test: host1, without SACK, which sends 100 bytes; the tap drops the segment once,
so only the timer can repair it. Observation: level 2, a timeout, and the smallest window is
two MSS, 2920 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: vegas
%# value: "TcpVegas"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassVegas")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMin("smallestCwnd", "value")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("numRtos").describe("the timeout").within(2.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 100")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{smallestCwnd} >= 2900 && {smallestCwnd} <= 2940")
             .describe("the ACK of the 100 bytes; the window after the timeout was two MSS")
             .within(6.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassVegas compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpVegas"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassVegas: PASS
